**`src/routes/api/public/hooks/sense-tick.ts:139-145`** — serial connector fan-out, one workspace at a time, one connector at a time:
```ts
for (const c of PULL_INGESTORS) {
  const r = await c.ingest(ws.owner_id, ws.id).catch(() => null);   // awaited serially
  connectors[c.provider] = { inserted: r?.inserted ?? 0, source: r?.source ?? "none" };
}
```
Fix — the ingestors are independent per-provider calls, so parallelize:
```ts
const results = await Promise.all(
  PULL_INGESTORS.map((c) => c.ingest(ws.owner_id, ws.id).catch(() => null)),
);
PULL_INGESTORS.forEach((c, i) => {
  connectors[c.provider] = { inserted: results[i]?.inserted ?? 0, source: results[i]?.source ?? "none" };
});
```

**`src/routes/api/public/hooks/sense-tick.ts:214-236`** (`tagUntaggedSignals`) — up to `MAX_TAG_UPDATES` serial per-row `UPDATE`s in a loop:
```ts
for (const row of data) {
  ...
  await supabaseAdmin.from("signals").update({ tags: u.tags, sentiment: u.sentiment }).eq("id", row.id);
}
```
Fix — collect the changed rows and `upsert` in one batch call instead of one round-trip per row.

**`src/routes/api/public/hooks/resume-runs.ts:245-258`** — two serial `count` queries (`mission_steps`, then `agent_runs`) issued *per candidate mission* inside a `for` loop. The file already has a `buildGateMaps`-style batching helper elsewhere that isn't reused here. Fix — pull both counts for the whole candidate batch in two `IN (...)` queries up front, build a `Map<missionId, {stepCount, activeRuns}>`, then loop over the map instead of hitting the DB per mission.

**`src/components/governance/ApprovalsPanel.tsx:148-155`** — filter/sort chains rebuilt on every render regardless of whether `q.data` changed:
```ts
const all = q.data?.approvals ?? [];
const pending = all.filter((a) => a.status === "pending").sort(...);
const resolved = all.filter((a) => a.status !== "pending");
const rows = [...pending, ...resolved];
```
Fix:
```ts
const { rows, pending, lowRisk } = useMemo(() => {
  const all = q.data?.approvals ?? [];
  const pending = all.filter((a) => a.status === "pending")
    .sort((x, y) => (x.expires_at ?? "9999").localeCompare(y.expires_at ?? "9999"));
  const resolved = all.filter((a) => a.status !== "pending");
  return { rows: [...pending, ...resolved], pending, lowRisk: pending.filter((a) => a.risk === "low") };
}, [q.data]);
```

**`src/components/discover/SignalFeed.tsx:288-292`** — two derived counts (`thisWeekCount`, `unclusteredCount`) computed inline on every render, right next to sibling values in the same file that already use `useMemo`. Same fix pattern: fold into the existing memo or add a small one keyed on `signals.data`.

**`src/components/discover/CalendarPanel.tsx:936,1211`** — partially fixed. The expensive derivation (`allItems`/`feed`/`buckets`) is already in one `useMemo` (line 321), but `MonthGrid` and `YearGrid` are plain function components, not `React.memo`, and are called with fresh inline props/callbacks each render:
```tsx
<MonthGrid ... />         // line 729 — re-renders every parent render regardless of prop equality
<YearGrid buckets={buckets} />  // line 740
```
Fix — wrap both in `React.memo`, and make sure any callback props passed to them are themselves stable (`useCallback`), otherwise the memo does nothing.

**`src/lib/connectors/resolve.server.ts:249-436`** (`resolveProviderAuth`) — this is the one still open. Only the workspace `plan_tier` lookup got a cache (5-min TTL, lines 79-90); the rest of the function's 2-4 sequential credential-chain queries (product binding → workspace binding → user connection → env fallback) re-run in full on **every tool call within a run**, even though the result doesn't change mid-run. A parallel fix already landed for a different cache (BYOK key resolution, commit `71c9ce03`, `KeyResolutionCache` threaded through `ToolCtx`) — the same pattern applies here and wasn't applied to this file:
```ts
// runtime.server.ts already does this for key resolution:
const keyResolutionCache: KeyResolutionCache = {};
// resolve.server.ts needs the equivalent: a per-run cache object created
// once in loop.server.ts, threaded through ToolCtx, keyed by
// `${provider}:${workspaceId}:${productId}` so resolveProviderAuth short-circuits
// after the first resolution per run instead of re-querying every tool call.
```

**`src/components/knowledge/ImpactLedgerPanel.tsx:85`** — untracked `setTimeout` in `copyMarkdown`, no cleanup, no dedup:
```ts
setTimeout(() => setCopied(false), 1600);
```
If the component unmounts (or the user clicks copy twice) before 1.6s elapses, this either sets state on an unmounted component or leaves stale overlapping timers. Fix:
```ts
const copyTimerRef = useRef<ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>>();
async function copyMarkdown(markdown: string) {
  try {
    await navigator.clipboard.writeText(markdown);
    setCopied(true);
    clearTimeout(copyTimerRef.current);
    copyTimerRef.current = setTimeout(() => setCopied(false), 1600);
  } catch { /* clipboard unavailable */ }
}
useEffect(() => () => clearTimeout(copyTimerRef.current), []);
```

